      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Seventh chord",
      "body": "Stack one more 3rd on top of a triad and you get a **seventh chord**: root, 3rd, 5th and 7th. On C, using only notes of C major, that is C E G B.\n\n**Why it matters:** Jazz, soul, R&B and lots of pop use 7th chords instead of plain triads. They sound fuller and smoother.",
